# Shaolin Nym / Nim — ancient Dolbluth architect, S3E11

**ACTUALLY PHYSICALLY ENCOUNTERED [S3E11](../../episodes/S3E11.md)** at formerly sealed three-hollow triangle gate. Name heard as **Shaolin Nym (Parakeet) / Nim (Qwen)**, orthography **ASR PROVISIONAL**. **Dolbluth/Dobluth** culture spelling similarly uncertain. She emerges when Koh, Evelyn, Krandal **ACTUALLY INSERT bat, grick, hook-horror urns**. An ancient **female mummy figure**, skin shrunk and cracked like leather, **very long dense matted hair down below buttocks with spiders actively weaving inside**, near-shredded thin linen remnants, face narrow and gaunt. NOT a living current woman, regal elf in pristine clothing or magical winged figure. **Speaks in language only translated into the original heroes' minds**; other expedition members draw weapons and cannot understand the telepathic conversation. On realizing original Delvers seek liberation rather than dark master, **bows low on all fours**, offering old lore.

**Her NPC HISTORICAL CLAIMS:** She served as **architect of Dolbluth outcasts** and says Emperor **Orgoth Argus/Argir**, identified with Khalazar, betrayed the Seldarine and suppressed gods/earlier kings thousands of years ago. Outcasts imprisoned him beyond gate. About a thousand years ago predecessors dismantled his machines but he returned. She instructs heroes to **take THREE organ urns, rebuild Khalazar in true form, supply SINGLE DROP ANCESTRAL DOLBLUTH BLOOD**, and kill true form permanently, pointing to **Koh's red crystal blood wrist device**. **Not yet corroborated ancient history, and organ-reassembly/blood ritual NOT performed in S3E11**. Neither Dolbluth lineage nor exact blood assay independently verified; previous aboleth remarks comparable but do not prove full mechanics.

**ACTUAL resolution:** She motions to gate, **three urns physically LIFT out of hollows and gate OPENS**, her fingers/arms fall to powder, whole body crumbles to dust. She does NOT enter dunes with party, fight bat or resurrect. Koh ACCEPTS the released urns but no explicit stow described. Door ACTUALLY shuts again after expedition passes into dunes. **She is physically gone at current cutoff**, not a recurrent travelling companion. [Three-urn register](../items/three-urns-triangle-gate.md) · [altar](../places/triangle-gate-catacombs.md) · [P/Q report](../../../reports/DELVERS_S3E11_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-26.md). Original audio/written D&D name sources not checked.
